[{"body":"## Useless assignment to local variable

The value assigned to terminalAuditAttempted here is unused.

---

General fix: remove assignments to local variables when the assigned value is never subsequently read, unless needed for side effects (not applicable to primitive assignment).</p>
<p>Best fix here: in <code>packages/admin/src/dispatcher.ts</code>, remove the single redundant assignment <code>terminalAuditAttempted = true;</code> inside the error-handling audit-write branch. This does not change behavior because:</p>
<ul>
<li>the only relevant guard using <code>terminalAuditAttempted</code> in this shown block is already evaluated before the assignment,</li>
<li>downstream result/idempotency logic depends on <code>terminalAuditWritten</code> and <code>auditId</code>, not <code>terminalAuditAttempted</code>.</li>
</ul>
