{"author":"chatgpt-codex-connector[bot]","created_at":"2026-08-21T16:01:33Z","html_url":"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3831751943","id":3831751943,"line":56,"original_line":56,"path":"searchfn/admin/src/domain-service.ts","review_id":4995156271,"summary":"**\u003csub\u003e\u003csub\u003e![P1 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P1-orange?style=flat)\u003c/sub\u003e\u003c/sub\u003e  Preserve numeric-looking string document IDs** | For a composite target such as `orders:001`, this converts the document ID from the string `\"001\"` to the number `1`. Single-document indexing therefore targets a different ID than batch indexing, which preserves string IDs, and `remove-document` can delete numeric document `1` instead of string document `\"001\"`. Preserve the ID suffix as a string or carry explicit ID-type information in the input. | Useful? React with 👍 / 👎.","updated_at":"2026-08-21T16:01:33Z"}
{"author":"chatgpt-codex-connector[bot]","created_at":"2026-08-21T16:01:33Z","html_url":"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3831751947","id":3831751947,"line":110,"original_line":110,"path":"searchfn/admin/src/domain-service.ts","review_id":4995156271,"summary":"**\u003csub\u003e\u003csub\u003e![P2 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P2-yellow?style=flat)\u003c/sub\u003e\u003c/sub\u003e  Apply the declared index-list query parameters** | When an installation has many configured indexes or the console supplies search/filter/pagination input, `listIndexes` ignores the entire input and always returns every index with `nextCursor: null`. This contradicts the operation's cursor-pagination declaration and makes the resource-list search UI return unrelated entries while bypassing the declared 200-item maximum; honor `limit`, `cursor`, and the advertised query fields before building the result. | Useful? React with 👍 / 👎.","updated_at":"2026-08-21T16:01:33Z"}
{"author":"pullfrog[bot]","created_at":"2026-08-21T16:08:47Z","html_url":"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3831799619","id":3831799619,"line":612,"original_line":612,"path":"superconsole/src/lib/server/super-console.ts","review_id":4995209775,"summary":"**Security:** Mutation authorization is selected from the HTTP method rather than the matched operation's safety classification. Capability validation currently allows a `GET` route whose classification is `write` or `destructive`, so that operation is dispatched without `authorizeMutation` (and therefore without provider CSRF/re-auth checks). Please either reject non-read operations on safe HTTP methods during manifest validation or authorize after matching based on `entry.operation.safety.classification`.","updated_at":"2026-08-21T16:08:48Z"}
{"author":"pullfrog[bot]","created_at":"2026-08-21T16:08:47Z","html_url":"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3831799625","id":3831799625,"line":68,"original_line":68,"path":"plugfn/admin/src/domain-service.ts","review_id":4995209775,"summary":"**Security:** These ownership predicates omit `tenantId`, even though `PlugFnDomainIdentity`, connections/installations, and `ownerFor()` carry it, and PlugFn core's `connectionMatchesActor()` requires exact tenant equality. If the same user or organization ID exists in two tenants, an admin mapped to tenant A can supply a tenant-B record ID and pass these checks (notably allowing `connections.refresh(id)`). Please include tenant equality in the direct-ID connection, installation, delegated, and legacy ownership checks and add a same-owner/different-tenant test.","updated_at":"2026-08-21T16:08:48Z"}
{"author":"pullfrog[bot]","created_at":"2026-08-21T16:08:47Z","html_url":"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3831799628","id":3831799628,"line":5,"original_line":5,"path":"superconsole/src/routes/[...missing]/+page.ts","review_id":4995209775,"summary":"This does not pass the package's own typecheck: `npm run typecheck --workspace superconsole` reports that `code` is not part of SvelteKit's `Error`, followed by two errors where `+error.svelte` reads `page.error.code` and `.details`. Please declare the intended `App.Error` shape in `src/app.d.ts` (or restrict these routes to the standard error shape) so the checked package is type-safe.","updated_at":"2026-08-21T16:08:48Z"}
{"author":"pullfrog[bot]","created_at":"2026-08-21T16:08:47Z","html_url":"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3831799631","id":3831799631,"line":9,"original_line":9,"path":"superconsole/src/lib/components/admin-api.ts","review_id":4995209775,"summary":"`SuperConsoleOptions.apiBasePath` changes the only prefix accepted by the server, but every bundled UI loader/action uses this hard-coded prefix. Configuring, for example, `/internal/admin` therefore makes the server reject all UI requests with 404. Please propagate the configured base path to the client/UI (including sign-in and download links), or remove/limit the option so a supported configuration cannot break the console.","updated_at":"2026-08-21T16:08:48Z"}
