{"comments":[{"author":"pullfrog","createdAt":"2026-08-21T16:08:47Z","id":"PRRC_kwDOP-e7KM7kZJ9D","line":612,"originalLine":612,"outdated":false,"summary":"**Security:** Mutation authorization is selected from the HTTP method rather than the matched operation's safety classification. Capability validation currently allows a `GET` route whose classification is `write` or `destructive`, so that operation is dispatched without `authorizeMutation` (and therefore without provider CSRF/re-auth checks). Please either reject non-read operations on safe HTTP methods during manifest validation or authorize after matching based on `entry.operation.safety.classification`.","updatedAt":"2026-08-21T16:08:48Z","url":"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3831799619"}],"id":"PRRT_kwDOP-e7KM6bN3yj","isOutdated":false,"isResolved":false,"line":612,"originalLine":612,"path":"superconsole/src/lib/server/super-console.ts"}
{"comments":[{"author":"pullfrog","createdAt":"2026-08-21T16:08:47Z","id":"PRRC_kwDOP-e7KM7kZJ9J","line":68,"originalLine":68,"outdated":false,"summary":"**Security:** These ownership predicates omit `tenantId`, even though `PlugFnDomainIdentity`, connections/installations, and `ownerFor()` carry it, and PlugFn core's `connectionMatchesActor()` requires exact tenant equality. If the same user or organization ID exists in two tenants, an admin mapped to tenant A can supply a tenant-B record ID and pass these checks (notably allowing `connections.refresh(id)`). Please include tenant equality in the direct-ID connection, installation, delegated, and legacy ownership checks and add a same-owner/different-tenant test.","updatedAt":"2026-08-21T16:08:48Z","url":"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3831799625"}],"id":"PRRT_kwDOP-e7KM6bN3ym","isOutdated":false,"isResolved":false,"line":68,"originalLine":68,"path":"plugfn/admin/src/domain-service.ts"}
{"comments":[{"author":"pullfrog","createdAt":"2026-08-21T16:08:47Z","id":"PRRC_kwDOP-e7KM7kZJ9M","line":5,"originalLine":5,"outdated":false,"summary":"This does not pass the package's own typecheck: `npm run typecheck --workspace superconsole` reports that `code` is not part of SvelteKit's `Error`, followed by two errors where `+error.svelte` reads `page.error.code` and `.details`. Please declare the intended `App.Error` shape in `src/app.d.ts` (or restrict these routes to the standard error shape) so the checked package is type-safe.","updatedAt":"2026-08-21T16:08:48Z","url":"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3831799628"}],"id":"PRRT_kwDOP-e7KM6bN3yo","isOutdated":false,"isResolved":false,"line":5,"originalLine":5,"path":"superconsole/src/routes/[...missing]/+page.ts"}
{"comments":[{"author":"pullfrog","createdAt":"2026-08-21T16:08:47Z","id":"PRRC_kwDOP-e7KM7kZJ9P","line":9,"originalLine":9,"outdated":false,"summary":"`SuperConsoleOptions.apiBasePath` changes the only prefix accepted by the server, but every bundled UI loader/action uses this hard-coded prefix. Configuring, for example, `/internal/admin` therefore makes the server reject all UI requests with 404. Please propagate the configured base path to the client/UI (including sign-in and download links), or remove/limit the option so a supported configuration cannot break the console.","updatedAt":"2026-08-21T16:08:48Z","url":"https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3831799631"}],"id":"PRRT_kwDOP-e7KM6bN3yt","isOutdated":false,"isResolved":false,"line":9,"originalLine":9,"path":"superconsole/src/lib/components/admin-api.ts"}
