    {
      "body": "**Security:** These ownership predicates omit `tenantId`, even though `PlugFnDomainIdentity`, connections/installations, and `ownerFor()` carry it, and PlugFn core's `connectionMatchesActor()` requires exact tenant equality. If the same user or organization ID exists in two tenants, an admin mapped to tenant A can supply a tenant-B record ID and pass these checks (notably allowing `connections.refresh(id)`). Please include tenant equality in the direct-ID connection, installation, delegated, and legacy ownership checks and add a same-owner/different-tenant test.",
      "created_at": "2026-08-21T16:08:47Z",
      "html_url": "https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3831799625",
