      "body": "<!-- cubic:review-summary:start -->\n**40 issues found** across 1779 files\n<!-- cubic:review-summary:end -->\n\n**Not reviewed** (too large): `uifn/components/fixtures/data-rich/data-table.fixture.json` (~60,040 lines), `uifn/components/fixtures/data-rich/command.fixture.json` (~5,037 lines) - if these are generated or fixture files, add them to ignored paths to exclude them from future reviews.\n\n<details>\n<summary>Prompt for AI agents (unresolved issues)</summary>\n\n```text\n\nCheck if these issues are valid — if so, understand the root cause of each and fix them. If appropriate, use sub-agents to investigate and fix each issue separately.\n\n\n<file name=\"uifn/core/scripts/build.mjs\">\n\n<violation number=\"1\" location=\"uifn/core/scripts/build.mjs:24\">\nP1: When the build reaches `accordion`, it asks tsup to bundle nonexistent `createAccordionController`, so the build fails before producing any public primitive entrypoints. Add the missing controller exports or map catalog entries to verified source exports before bundling.</violation>\n</file>\n\n<file name=\"superconsole/src/routes/audit/+page.ts\">\n\n<violation number=\"1\" location=\"superconsole/src/routes/audit/+page.ts:12\">\nP1: The audit endpoint returns raw `AdminAuditEvent` objects, but this loader forwards them as `AuditEventViewModel` without mapping. Audit rows therefore read undefined `occurredAt`/`actor`/`action`, render the object target as `[object Object]`, and show raw outcomes as `Unknown`; map each event to the UI view model and normalize its outcome and target.</violation>\n</file>\n\n<file name=\"uifn/core/src/algorithms/id.ts\">\n\n<violation number=\"1\" location=\"uifn/core/src/algorithms/id.ts:12\">\nP1: Distinct collection values can normalize to the same ID, and non-ASCII-only values can make part rendering throw. Encode dynamic segments reversibly or add a collision-resistant suffix instead of using this lossy slug as the unique ID segment.</violation>\n</file>\n\n<file name=\"mcpfn/core/src/errors.ts\">\n\n<violation number=\"1\" location=\"mcpfn/core/src/errors.ts:16\">\nP1: When error details contain a throwing `toJSON` or Proxy trap, `jsonSafe` returns a string for the entire response envelope. `errorResult` then emits that string as `structuredContent`, so the MCP response can be rejected as invalid and the stable error code/message are lost; serialize details independently or return a safe object envelope on failure.</violation>\n</file>\n\n<file name=\"uifn/adapter-kit/src/refs.ts\">\n\n<violation number=\"1\" location=\"uifn/adapter-kit/src/refs.ts:55\">\nP1: When a key is re-registered before the earlier registration cleans up, the earlier cleanup deletes the newer element. Make cleanup conditional on its registration token so an old component cannot unregister the current element.</violation>\n\n<violation number=\"2\" location=\"uifn/adapter-kit/src/refs.ts:66\">\nP2: When `TElement` is a valid falsy value such as `''`, `require` throws even though `register` and `has` report it present. Check map membership instead of element truthiness.</violation>\n</file>\n\n<file name=\"uifn/core/src/algorithms/selection.ts\">\n\n<violation number=\"1\" location=\"uifn/core/src/algorithms/selection.ts:26\">\nP2: `Object.freeze` does not prevent `Set` mutations, so JavaScript consumers can change `selection.selectedKeys` in place despite the readonly immutable contract. Return a genuinely read-only set facade or use an immutable representation for `selectedKeys`.</violation>\n\n<violation number=\"2\" location=\"uifn/core/src/algorithms/selection.ts:50\">\nP2: When `toKey` is not in the collection, this branch still computes a range with `indexOf(toKey) === -1` and returns a selection whose `currentKey` is missing, potentially clearing the current selection. Validate membership before range calculations and return the existing selection for an invalid target.</violation>\n\n<violation number=\"3\" location=\"uifn/core/src/algorithms/selection.ts:51\">\nP2: When a collection uses numeric key `0` as the anchor, this truthiness check discards it and shift-selecting starts at `toKey`, selecting only the target instead of the full range. Check the anchor against `null` explicitly.</violation>\n</file>\n\n<file name=\"uifn/core/src/algorithms/locale.ts\">\n\n<violation number=\"1\" location=\"uifn/core/src/algorithms/locale.ts:18\">\nP2: When collation-equivalent text uses combining marks or expansions, `startsWith` and `includes` slice by code-point count and compare the wrong window. Match over collation-element boundaries or candidate string boundaries instead of using `normalizedQuery.length`.</violation>\n</file>\n\n<file name=\"uifn/core/src/algorithms/color.ts\">\n\n<violation number=\"1\" location=\"uifn/core/src/algorithms/color.ts:23\">\nP2: When a malformed numeric token reaches `parseUIFnColor`, the regex matches it and the parser stores `NaN` in the color, producing invalid serialized values. Use a strict CSS-number pattern and reject non-finite parsed channels before constructing the color.</violation>\n</file>\n\n<file name=\"uifn/components/src/contracts.ts\">\n\n<violation number=\"1\" location=\"uifn/components/src/contracts.ts:12\">\nP2: Checkbox indeterminate state is not representable with this contract: the type accepts `mixed` but rejects canonical `indeterminate`, while the recipe emits the value unchanged and the stylesheet targets `data-state=\"indeterminate\"`. Add the canonical `indeterminate` value and align this union with the catalog/core state names.</violation>\n</file>\n\n<file name=\"uifn/core/src/algorithms/range.ts\">\n\n<violation number=\"1\" location=\"uifn/core/src/algorithms/range.ts:11\">\nP2: When a range step uses scientific notation with a fractional mantissa, `decimals` undercounts its precision and `alignRangeValue` changes valid step values. Compute decimal precision from both the mantissa and exponent.</violation>\n\n<violation number=\"2\" location=\"uifn/core/src/algorithms/range.ts:22\">\nP2: When `step` is `NaN` or `Infinity`, this guard accepts it and `alignRangeValue` publishes `NaN`. Reject non-finite steps before calculating the aligned value.</violation>\n\n<violation number=\"3\" location=\"uifn/core/src/algorithms/range.ts:30\">\nP2: For valid ranges finer than twelve decimal places, the precision cap rounds aligned values to a different step. Preserve the definition's precision or reject unsupported precision explicitly before rounding.</violation>\n\n<violation number=\"4\" location=\"uifn/core/src/algorithms/range.ts:55\">\nP2: When `max - min` is not divisible by `step`, End returns an unaligned maximum while normalization and percent conversion return the previous step. Apply one consistent endpoint policy or reject non-divisible range definitions.</violation>\n</file>\n\n<file name=\"uifn/core/src/algorithms/async-list.ts\">\n\n<violation number=\"1\" location=\"uifn/core/src/algorithms/async-list.ts:31\">\nP2: When a subscriber throws during the loading notification, `load()` rejects before invoking the loader and later subscribers are skipped. Isolate subscriber callbacks so one listener cannot abort list operations.</violation>\n\n<violation number=\"2\" location=\"uifn/core/src/algorithms/async-list.ts:54\">\nP2: When `cancel()` is called without immediately starting another load, it aborts the request but leaves the list visibly `loading` forever. Publish a non-loading state when canceling the active request.</violation>\n</file>\n\n<file name=\"superconsole/examples/dev-installation.ts\">\n\n<violation number=\"1\" location=\"superconsole/examples/dev-installation.ts:72\">\nP1: When this module is loaded directly via `SUPERCONSOLE_INSTALLATION`, the installation loader invokes its similarly named factory without arguments, so startup throws before creating the console. Export a no-argument deployment wrapper, or rename this options-taking helper so it cannot be selected as the