yAdapter` distinguishes numeric and string IDs, so the document remains searchable while this service reports success; preserve the ID type or make removal handle both representations.</violation>\n</file>\n\n<file name=\"uifn/core/src/primitives/legacy-compat.ts\">\n\n<violation number=\"1\" location=\"uifn/core/src/primitives/legacy-compat.ts:23\">\nP2: When any subscriber throws, `update` has already replaced `state` but aborts the loop and propagates the exception, so later subscribers miss the transition. Wrap each callback in `try/catch` to isolate subscriber failures.</violation>\n\n<violation number=\"2\" location=\"uifn/core/src/primitives/legacy-compat.ts:35\">\nP2: `createLegacyAvatar` never emits the current state to a newly subscribed callback, so a subscriber that reads after subscribing sees nothing until a later `setLoading`/`setLoaded`/`setError` transition. Controllers in this codebase (`createUIFnController` at uifn/core/src/controller.ts:412) and Svelte-store-backed adapters deliver the initial state on subscribe, so a consumer relying on the initial 'idle' state will render stale/empty until an action fires. Invoke the callback with the current `state` inside `subscribe` (before adding it to the set, defensively) to match that contract.</violation>\n</file>\n\n<file name=\"superconsole/src/lib/components/resource-pages.ts\">\n\n<violation number=\"1\" location=\"superconsole/src/lib/components/resource-pages.ts:81\">\nP2: When a registered manifest uses `constructor`, `prototype`, or `__proto__` in a query path, this guard throws before the request can produce an admin error view. Reject reserved path segments during manifest validation, or catch this construction error in `loadResourceList` so the resource page does not fail unexpectedly.</violation>\n</file>\n\n<file name=\"superconsole/scripts/verify-function-agnostic.mjs\">\n\n<violation number=\"1\" location=\"superconsole/scripts/verify-function-agnostic.mjs:39\">\nP3: Search indices are computed on `source.toLowerCase()` but then used to index the original `source`. `toLowerCase()` is not length-preserving (e.g. 'İ' becomes two code units), and a single such character misaligns every subsequent index between `lower` and `source`, yielding wrong region content and lineOffsets in the guard. Search for openings/closings on `source` (case-insensitively per tag) or validate the two buffers have equal length before mixing their indices.</violation>\n\n<violation number=\"2\" location=\"superconsole/scripts/verify-function-agnostic.mjs:51\">\nP2: When a valid Svelte script contains a string such as `'</scriptx>'` or `'</script'`, this scan treats it as the closing tag and drops later code from analysis. Match a complete `</script>` end tag, including optional whitespace, before slicing the region.</violation>\n</file>\n\n<file name=\"uifn/core/scripts/build.mjs\">\n\n<violation number=\"1\" location=\"uifn/core/scripts/build.mjs:13\">\nP2: The generated wildcard primitive entries now reintroduce removed `createX` APIs, contradicting the package’s breaking-no-shims contract. Remove these aliases, or update the migration manifest and compatibility contract to document their incompatible legacy behavior.</violation>\n</file>\n\n<file name=\"uifn/svelte/tests/phase-14-ssr-hydration.mjs\">\n\n<violation number=\"1\" location=\"uifn/svelte/tests/phase-14-ssr-hydration.mjs:83\">\nP2: The catch block drops the error entirely: ssrFixStacktrace(cause) is now a no-op whose result is unused, and the cause is neither sent to the client nor logged. When a request fails, the test just sees 'Internal Server Error' (HTTP 500) with no record of the underlying error, forcing a reproduce to debug. Log the cause server-side before ending the response.</violation>\n</file>\n\n<file name=\"mcpfn/core/src/canonical.ts\">\n\n<violation number=\"1\" location=\"mcpfn/core/src/canonical.ts:33\">\nP2: `canonicalJson` re-enters `toJSON` on the returned value and passes no property key. Invoke each hook once with its current key, then serialize the returned value without reapplying `toJSON`; apply the same guard in `canonicalize`.</violation>\n\n<violation number=\"2\" location=\"mcpfn/core/src/canonical.ts:40\">\nP2: When a manifest value contains a sparse array, `entry.map(...)` skips its holes and `join` emits empty fields, causing distinct arrays to produce the same canonical JSON. Iterate by index so missing elements serialize as `null`.</violation>\n</file>\n\n<file name=\"uifn/core/src/algorithms/async-list.ts\">\n\n<violation number=\"1\" location=\"uifn/core/src/algorithms/async-list.ts:62\">\nP2: If an abort handler starts another `load()`, this block cancels that replacement request because `abort()` dispatches synchronously and `load()` replaces `controller` first. Capture the canceled controller and publish only while it remains current.</violation>\n</file>\n\n<file name=\"uifn/core/src/algorithms/locale.ts\">\n\n<violation number=\"1\" location=\"uifn/core/src/algorithms/locale.ts:30\">\nP2: When an editable selection searches long item labels, `includes` enumerates every substring and rebuilds each candidate, causing multi-second UI stalls for a nonmatching query. Replace the exhaustive substring allocation with a bounded or near-linear collation search that still handles collation expansions.</violation>\n</file>\n\n<file name=\"packages/admin/src/registry.ts\">\n\n<violation number=\"1\" location=\"packages/admin/src/registry.ts:39\">\nP3: This diff introduces a second copy of the route method/path parser. validator.ts `operationRoutePath` now implements the identical manual whitespace-splitting loop with the same verb allowlist, and two other consumers still parse routes differently with a regex (`routeMatches` in registry.ts line 234 and `route()` in openapi.ts line 71, both `trim().split(/\\s+/, 1)[0]`). Four places now derive `method`/`path` from a string route with three distinct implementations that must stay in sync; a future change to one (e.g. method normalization or path handling) can silently diverge the registry route, validation, matching, and OpenAPI generation. Extract the split-and-validate logic into a single shared helper in this package and use it from `routeOf`, `operationRoutePath`, `routeMatches`, and `route`.</violation>\n</file>\n```\n\n</details>\n\n<sub>Reply with feedback, questions, or to request a fix.<br /><br />[Re-trigger cubic](https://www.cubic.dev/action/re-review/pr/21nCo/super-functions/116/ai_pr_review_1787367056771_267b63b5-9188-46fd-83de-8b2d5628a52a?returnTo=https%3A%2F%2Fgithub.com%2F21nCo%2Fsuper-functions%2Fpull%2F116)</sub>\n\n<!-- cubic:review-post:ai_pr_review_1787367056771_267b63b5-9188-46fd-83de-8b2d5628a52a:8d16f12d9a673cbed04f6c20cc9a06b0e770389e:e23e6324-2c6c-4e6a-843e-4e4bd3612e24 -->"
