      "comment": {
        "author": "chatgpt-codex-connector",
        "createdAt": "2026-08-22T08:13:59Z",
        "url": "https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3835590713",
        "body": "**<sub><sub>![P2 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P2-yellow?style=flat)</sub></sub>  Include CSRF metadata for POST read operations**\n\nFor a read-classified operation that uses an unsafe HTTP method, such as `apifn.specs.compare` (`POST`), `SuperConsole.handle` still calls `authorizeMutation` based on the request method, so cookie-authenticated AuthFn requests require the provider CSRF header. This classification check omits that header from OpenAPI, causing generated clients or API-console requests that follow the document to receive a CSRF 403; determine CSRF metadata from the HTTP method instead.\n\nUseful? React with 👍 / 👎.",
        "commit": "94c8cc31b8ac30dfffc7126102cca8f024c28cb2"
      }
    },
    {
      "path": "filefn/admin/src/index.ts",
      "line": 185,
      "isOutdated": false,
      "comment": {
        "author": "chatgpt-codex-connector",
        "createdAt": "2026-08-22T08:13:59Z",
        "url": "https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3835590707",
        "body": "**<sub><sub>![P1 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P1-orange?style=flat)</sub></sub>  Return usable FileFn download descriptors**\n\nWhen either download operation is invoked through the dispatcher, declaring `url` and `headers` as output fields causes `redactAdminOutputValue` to replace the signed URL and any required headers with `\"[REDACTED]\"`. The REST, MCP, and typed SDK responses therefore cannot be used to download the file; the artifact download declaration has the same defect. Return a provider-safe descriptor instead of redacting the fields that constitute the operation's result.\n\nUseful? React with 👍 / 👎.",
        "commit": "94c8cc31b8ac30dfffc7126102cca8f024c28cb2"
      }
    },
    {
      "path": "hostfn/admin/src/index.ts",
      "line": 736,
      "isOutdated": false,
      "comment": {
        "author": "chatgpt-codex-connector",
        "createdAt": "2026-08-22T07:57:05Z",
        "url": "https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3835561790",
        "body": "**<sub><sub>![P2 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P2-yellow?style=flat)</sub></sub>  Encode cursor payloads as UTF-8**\n\nWhen any active scope identifier contains a non-Latin-1 character and a HostFn list has another page, `btoa(JSON.stringify(...))` throws `InvalidCharacterError` while constructing `nextCursor`, causing an otherwise successful list request to fail. Admin scope validation permits arbitrary nonblank Unicode strings, so encode the JSON as UTF-8 bytes before base64 encoding and reverse that transformation when decoding.\n\nUseful? React with 👍 / 👎.",
        "commit": "94c8cc31b8ac30dfffc7126102cca8f024c28cb2"
      }
    },
    {
      "path": "mcpfn/core/src/registry.ts",
      "line": 183,
      "isOutdated": false,
      "comment": {
        "author": "chatgpt-codex-connector",
        "createdAt": "2026-08-22T07:57:05Z",
        "url": "https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3835561789",
        "body": "**<sub><sub>![P2 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P2-yellow?style=flat)</sub></sub>  Reject duplicate resource-template URI patterns**\n\nWhen two templates have different names but the same `uriTemplate`, this name-only duplicate check accepts both and advertises both from `resources/templates/list`. However, `matchResource` resolves by iterating the templates and returns the first URI match, so the later template's `read`, subscription, and completion behavior is unreachable. Reject duplicate `uriTemplate` values at registration time.\n\nUseful? React with 👍 / 👎.",
        "commit": "94c8cc31b8ac30dfffc7126102cca8f024c28cb2"
      }
    },
    {
      "path": "uifn/parity/src/trace.mjs",
      "line": 264,
      "isOutdated": false,
      "comment": {
        "author": "pullfrog",
        "createdAt": "2026-08-22T07:43:02Z",
        "url": "https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3835537185",
        "body": "[P1] Validate the expected action outcome rather than any activity. The vectors declare action names and callback names but no expected post-state, callback arguments, or DOM semantics, so changing an unrelated state key or invoking a callback with the wrong payload makes `observed` true; line 380 then reports `passed`, and the Svelte test only asserts that result. Encode and compare expected state/callback effects so behaviorally incorrect adapters cannot satisfy the parity gate.",
        "commit": "94c8cc31b8ac30dfffc7126102cca8f024c28cb2"
      }
    },
    {
      "path": "plugfn/admin/src/domain-service.ts",
      "line": 138,
      "isOutdated": false,
      "comment": {
        "author": "pullfrog",
        "createdAt": "2026-08-22T07:43:02Z",
        "url": "https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3835537182",
        "body": "[P1] Derive workflow tenant ownership from an authoritative field. `WorkflowEngine.create()` and `AdapterWorkflowStorage.create()` persist caller-provided `metadata` unchanged, and no core producer reserves or populates this key. As a result, ordinary/legacy workflows are hidden from administration, while any application path that accepts workflow metadata can forge the value used here for isolation. Add a first-class tenant owner populated from authenticated context (or verify through another authoritative relation) rather than treating generic metadata as authorization provenance.",
        "commit": "94c8cc31b8ac30dfffc7126102cca8f024c28cb2"
      }
    },
    {
      "path": "filefn/admin/src/index.ts",
      "line": 198,
      "isOutdated": false,
      "comment": {
        "author": "chatgpt-codex-connector",
        "createdAt": "2026-08-22T07:39:29Z",
        "url": "https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3835531570",
        "body": "**<sub><sub>![P2 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P2-yellow?style=flat)</sub></sub>  Do not bind share revocation to the hash prefix**\n\nFor each listed share link, the generic row-action binder uses the resource identity (`tokenHashPrefix`) as this operation's `token` input and hides that target field from the form. The operator therefore cannot supply the required original plaintext token, and every displayed Revoke Share action confirms and submits the hash prefix instead, so it cannot revoke the selected link; avoid projecting this as an identity-bound row action or provide an independently editable plaintext-token input.\n\nUseful? React with 👍 / 👎.",
        "commit": "94c8cc31b8ac30dfffc7126102cca8f024c28cb2"
      }
    },
    {
      "path": "filefn/admin/src/index.ts",
      "line": 37,
      "isOutdated": false,
      "comment": {
        "author": "chatgpt-codex-connector",
        "createdAt": "2026-08-22T07:39:29Z",
        "url": "https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3835531568",
        "body": "**<sub><sub>![P2 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P2-yellow?style=flat)</sub></sub>  Mark file-bound collections as non-standalone**\n\nOpening Versions from the FileFn module page invokes `filefn.versions.list` without the required `fileId`; Grants, Share Links, and Artifacts have the same problem. These resources omit `presentation.parent` and consequently default to `standaloneList: true`, so the console advertises cards that only return input-validation errors and cannot generate related links from a file detail page; declare their file-parent bindings and disable standalone listing.\n\nUseful? React with 👍 / 👎.",
        "commit": "94c8cc31b8ac30dfffc7126102cca8f024c28cb2"
      }
    },
    {
      "path": "datafn/admin/src/index.ts",
      "line": 485,
      "isOutdated": false,
      "comment": {
        "author": "chatgpt-codex-connector",
        "createdAt": "2026-08-22T07:39:29Z",
        "url": "https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/116#discussion_r3835531565",
        "body": "**<sub><sub>![P2 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P2-yellow?style=flat)</sub></sub>  Supply a resource selector before exposing Records**\n\nWhen an operator opens the DataFn Records card in Super Console, the generated list request contains no `filter`, because this resource declares neither presentation filters nor a parent binding. Requiring `filter` here therefore makes the default Records route fail validation on every visit, leaving record browsing unusable unless the operator manually constructs a JSON query parameter; add a control/binding for `filter.resource` or stop advertising this as a standalone list.\n\nUseful? React with 👍 / 👎.",
        "commit": "94c8cc31b8ac30dfffc7126102cca8f024c28cb2"
      }
    },
    {
      "path": "uifn/core/src/algorithms/locale.ts",
      "line": 91,
      "isOutdated": false,
      "comment": {
        "author": "cubic-dev-ai",
