        "body": "**<sub><sub>![P2 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P2-yellow?style=flat)</sub></sub>  Include CSRF metadata for POST read operations**\n\nFor a read-classified operation that uses an unsafe HTTP method, such as `apifn.specs.compare` (`POST`), `SuperConsole.handle` still calls `authorizeMutation` based on the request method, so cookie-authenticated AuthFn requests require the provider CSRF header. This classification check omits that header from OpenAPI, causing generated clients or API-console requests that follow the document to receive a CSRF 403; determine CSRF metadata from the HTTP method instead.\n\nUseful? React with 👍 / 👎.",
